<http://data.silknow.org/object/a8c81ace-2b2e-3f87-a8c4-f20748f532d7/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Woman’s petticoat of white silk satin, lined with cream-coloured glazed worsted and wadded with wool.  It is quilted in running stitch with white silk thread in a horizontal pattern of a leafy vine around the hem, with swags of zig-zag lines and large abstract thistles above.  The petticoat is made of 6 panels of silk with pocket openings in the side seams, bound with 1¼-inch (2.8 cm) wide ivory silk ribbon.  The same ribbon binds the hem.  There is a wide box pleat at centre front with side pleats and an inverted box pleat at centre back with side pleats.  The waist is bound with ⅞-inch (2.2 cm) wide unbleached linen tape, which forms the ties."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/a8c81ace-2b2e-3f87-a8c4-f20748f532d7> .

<http://data.silknow.org/actor/52b81c44-3e7b-3e93-8d22-39f899b485d6>
